WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.740
What’s happenin fam? This week we
peepin’ mad beauty with The Goldfinch by Donna Tartt.

00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:21.699
27 year old Theo Decker is holed up in an
Amsterdam Hotel, sick as a dog and sweatin

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:26.039
dat the po-po might bust in there any second.
And even though he don’t blame nobody but

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:30.609
hisself fo’ dis mess, he think he coulda
stayed on the righteous path if his mama wouldna

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:35.080
died fourteen years ago. Da majority of what
follows in this book is a flashback.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.570
When Theo was jus’ a lil G, he was hittin’
up an Art Museum wit his mama one day when

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.690
he peep game at two of da finest thangs he
ever seen- a red-head baby-girl name Pippa,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.450
and a painting called the Goldfinch. Brutha
can’t keep his eyes of dat dime when BOOM-

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:56.770
a bomb goes off killin almost errybody up
in there- including Theo’s mama. Damn!

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:02.590
When Theo come to, da old geezer who was rollin
wit Pippa, who named Welty, be all like “Uggh..Say

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:07.140
bruh. My white ass bout to die. Take this
ring and dat sh** over thurr.” Thinkin he

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:12.200
talkin bout da Goldfinch painting, Theo boosts
dat art and bounces befo’ da po-lice arrive.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.740
Since Theo don’t wanna hustle on da streets,
brutha shack up wit his boy Andy and his fam,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.870
the Barbours. One day, Theo finds Welty’s
old crew and returns the ring to his padna

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:27.050
Hobie. Hobie like “Preesh blood.” Theo
runs in to fine-ass Pippa there too, and he

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.520
find out dat explosion left her all kindsa
jacked up.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.140
Their reunion don’t last long, cuz Pippa
get shipped off to Texas even though Hobie

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.550
want her to stay. Still, ain’t all bad for
Theo, cuz Hobbie start schoolin him on how

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.860
to restore antiques up in his shop.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:46.990
Plus, Theo livin’ the ballas dream up at
da Barbour crib. But all dat go to sh** when

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.950
Theo’s high-as- balls pops, who walked out
on Theo and his mama back then, swang in to

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.490
town, scoop up Theo, and take him to live
with him in Vegas.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:00.630
Up in Sin City, Theo spend his nights smokin’
fatties wit his new friend Boris. Eventually

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:06.180
Theo’s deadbeat daddy try to steal all Theo’s
cash monies, and not long afta’ dat, dies

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.560
in a car crash.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.060
Theo know he gotta get da hell outta dodge
befo’ he get thrown in to foster care or

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.889
somethin’, so he packs up da Goldfinch and
peaces out to New York, where he hits up Hobie.

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:21.999
Turns out, booty-liscious Pippa there! But,
as always, their reunion don’t last long.

00:02:21.999 --> 00:02:27.689
8 years later, Theo hustlin w with Hobie slangin
antique up in his shop. Theo still got his

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:32.980
mind on Pippa 24/7, but she shacked up wit
some playa in London. Since Theo cain’t

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.879
have Pippa as his biddy, he get engaged to
Kitsey Barbour, one of Andy’s sisters.

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:42.870
Truth is- homeboy been up to no good lately.
Not only is he poppin’ pillz on the reg,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.139
but he been flippin FAKE antiques to people
like it ain’t no thang, and now some hater

00:02:47.139 --> 00:02:49.180
is tryna backmail him fo’ doin it.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:53.329
This dude- Lucius Reeve- even whip out da
big guns and say “I know you know where

00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:57.909
da Goldfinch is. Don’t MAKE me sick da fuzz
on yo ass.” Oh sh**.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:03.189
Then Theo find out a day before his engagement
party dat Kitsey still got it bad for some

00:03:03.189 --> 00:03:07.930
hood-ass brutha named Tom. And if that wasn’t
bad enough, Boris show up and say he jacked

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:13.079
The Goldfinch from Theo years ago and he been
usin’ it fo’ some shady deals dat yieldin’

00:03:13.079 --> 00:03:14.680
some PHAT stacks.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.489
Feelin’ like a real dick, Boris tell Theo
he wanna help him get it back. All they gotta

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:24.059
do is fly to Amsterdam and get it from the
dude who got it. Ain’t no thang, right?

00:03:24.059 --> 00:03:28.949
But when they get there, Boris pull out a
piece and start goin hyphy in this bitch.

00:03:28.949 --> 00:03:33.870
Eventually, Boris gets one in da arm and Theo
mercs a brutha, but some asshole gets outta

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:34.809
there with the painting.

00:03:34.809 --> 00:03:39.669
Thinkin they bout to get GOT by the law any
second now, Boris and Theo split up; Theo

00:03:39.669 --> 00:03:44.590
just lock himself in a hotel room, throwin’
back pillz, and marinatin on suicide. Outta

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:49.559
nowhere Boris come back and say “s’all
good baby. I sicked the cops on those haters

00:03:49.559 --> 00:03:54.809
and now we got a swole reward fo’ finding
da painting. Turn out, I actually led da 5-0

00:03:54.809 --> 00:04:00.299
to a whole buncha paintins, so we simmin in
change!” Now Theo in da clear with dat Reeve

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:01.019
fool too.

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:05.549
When Theo get back to New York, he comes clean
with Hobie bout selling slangin fake stuff,

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:10.199
then he start traveling the world makin things
right wit da people he played. In the end,

00:04:10.199 --> 00:04:15.719
he ain’t got Pippa, ain’t got the painting
and things ain’t so hot with Kitsey. Man.

00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:21.479
Sometimes loving beautiful things can be a
real sh** show.

00:04:21.479 --> 00:04:27.789
This book right hurr dun stirred up all sortsa
beef between critics. Some say it’s a buncha

00:04:27.789 --> 00:04:32.220
bullsh** frontin’ like it all profound,
while others sayin’ it’s da illest rhyme

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:37.509
to hit the shelves in years. So when it won
a Pulitzer in 2014, da haters REALLY started

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:42.509
hatin’ on a girl- but on the real, errybody
jus’ need to chill. This book got its share

00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:43.620
of literary swagger.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.370
Tha two dopest motifs are fo-sho mirrors and
da moon.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:51.949
Theo mentions a dream bout his mama at da
beginning of da book, and also at the end.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:55.319
And up in dream- world, Theo peepin her through
a mirror.

00:04:55.319 --> 00:04:59.599
Mirrors representin’ how da same thangs
happenin over and over, all cyclical n’

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:00.030
sh**.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:04.240
Fo’ example, Carel Fabritius, the thug who
painted “The Goldfinch” painting died

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.400
in an explosion. An ass-load of years later,
the painting almost get wrecked in another

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:14.129
explosion. This is what Theo’s mama callin
“A Time Warp.”- a.k.a- “a way of seeing

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:16.430
things twice, or more than twice.”

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.479
Also, Theo always bitchin bout how much of
a deadbeat scrub his daddy be. But Theo shouldn’t

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:26.650
be talkin mess, cuz he end up so strung out
an fu**ed up dat they basically doubles of

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.879
eachotha’- poppin pillz and gettin’ freak-nasty
with mo’ than one girl at a time.

00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:35.699
As for da moon, it usually representin da
tension between permanence and impermanence.

00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:39.430
Check it- Theo’s mama lay a story on Theo
dat her dad once told her:

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.770
“Daddy lifted me up on the fairgrounds and
told me to look at the moon. ‘When you feel

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.259
homesick,’ he said, ‘just look up. Because
the moon is the same wherever you go.’”

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:48.479
(254)

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:52.259
Thing is, after mama die and sh** start goin
south for ol’ Theo, he

00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:55.090
don’t actually see anythin’ familiar when
he peepin’ da moon:

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:59.189
“the only point of reference was the moon,
riding high above the clouds, which though

00:05:59.189 --> 00:06:03.250
bright and full seemed weirdly unstable somehow...not
the pure anchoring moon of the desert” (663)

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:08.900
So if da moon ain’t always da same like
mama say, then maybe NUTHIN’ stay the same

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:13.879
fo’eva. Matta’ fact, dat becomes one of
Theo’s main jams by da end of the book:

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:17.419
art gonna last foreva’ but the clock is
tickin’ fo human beings.

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:21.750
“For humans – trapped in biology – there
was no mercy: we lived a while, we fussed

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:27.159
around for a bit and died, we rotted in the
ground like garbage. Time destroyed us all

00:06:27.159 --> 00:06:28.030
soon enough. (695)

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:33.189
After beastin through the pain of death, rejection,
and drug addiction, Theo get real to’ up

00:06:33.189 --> 00:06:38.060
and realize dat humans ain’t nuthin mo’
than bags of meat that gonna rot one day.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:42.939
But dat painting, on the other hand, ain’t
got no expiration date on it. Unlike humans,

00:06:42.939 --> 00:06:47.400
objects- like the painting, Hobie’s Noah’s
Ark antique, and the Thug Notes book - gonna

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.969
keep flowin through history, creatin’ mad
meaning on its way.

00:06:50.969 --> 00:06:55.669
“It exists; and it keeps on existing. And
I add my own love to the history of people

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:57.550
who have loved beautiful things”

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.539
But since us humans jus’ shrivel up and
die so damn fast, life is jus’ straight

00:07:01.539 --> 00:07:05.520
up meaningless. Girl even give a shoutout
to my brutha Albert Camus

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.439
at da beginning of da book sayin: “The absurd
does not liberate. It binds.”

00:07:09.439 --> 00:07:13.740
Look, ain’t no doubt there was a lotta thought
put in do this piece, but to be honest, it

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:18.639
ain’t really my thing. I mean, if life is
absurd, then Theo cain’t be sayin’ sh**

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:23.999
like da world is a “catastrophic cesspool.”
Dat sound mo’ like extreme pessimism than

00:07:23.999 --> 00:07:25.159
absurdism to this thug.

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:29.110
But dat don’t mean there’s anything wrong
with people liking it. It’s just different

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:33.960
strokes fo’ different folks. So let me drop
a time warp on yo ass and say again: this

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.740
book ain’t ALL bullsh**, so don’t let
the haters tell you otherwise. But that bein

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.330
said, if you wanna check out a new book dat’s
impressive as HELL, watch me break down Gone

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:48.710
Girl by Gillian Flynn by clicking here. And
yo- don’t forget to claim to own copy of

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:54.020
da Thug Notes book. Coming out August 18.
Get ‘em while they’re hot. Ya head? Peace!

